  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What is the missing number?\n\n$\\,$ $\\boxed{}\\,%$ of $5=3$",
  "worked_solution": "We can write the given problem as the following product:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%\\times 5=3\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%=3÷5=\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{3\\times 20}{5\\times 20}=\\frac{60}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{60}{100}=60%\n$$",
